[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412275732","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111735#issuecomment-3412275732","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111735","id":3412275732,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LYzIU","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T18:29:44Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T18:31:13Z","body":"Copying my answer from the discussion for posterity:\n\n___\n\nWe should make it so the project manager window is maximized on startup on small displays instead (real window height including border >= screen height - `48 * EDSCALE` pixels[^1]), so that it's guaranteed to never cut off. The default height is fine on displays with a larger screen real estate, and reducing it would be a shame.\n\n[^1]: This is roughly the height of the Windows 10/11 task bar with the default settings.\n\n> Also, it would be great if there were a way to fine-tune the scale further - perhaps in 10% increments.\n\nThis can be done if you set the editor display scale to **Custom**, and adjust the custom display scale editor setting just below.\n\nThis is only available after opening the editor though, not in the project manager's quick settings menu.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412275732/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3472485020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111735#issuecomment-3472485020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111735","id":3472485020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7O-eqc","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-31T10:50:34Z","updated_at":"2025-10-31T10:50:34Z","body":"- Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103637 (or maybe duplicate)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3472485020/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3524418114","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111735#issuecomment-3524418114","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111735","id":3524418114,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SElpC","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T00:01:51Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T00:06:32Z","body":"I've tested this behavior on Linux (KDE X11). It appears the project manager window already maximizes itself if the screen resolution is too low to accomodate for the project manager's default window size. This occurs regardless of whether the taskbar is configured to automatically hide or not.\n\n(I tested this by changing the display resolution to 1024×768 at 100% scaling.)\n\n**Edit:** I can reproduce the issue on Windows 11 24H2, again at 1024×768 with 100% scaling. The issue occurs even with taskbar autohide (the window title will barely be visible). It's probably related to different DisplayServer behavior when using `window_set_size()` with a size greater than the screen resolution.\n\nThis should be fixed at the DisplayServer level, so that the behavior is consistent across all platforms and Godot projects also benefit from the fix.\n\ncc @bruvzg ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3524418114/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]